  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've verified your account, Ms. Laurent, and checked the delivery records for all four orders. Here's what I found:\n\n**#6501 \u2013 Saffron Lane (tonight): $25.00 credit added**\nIt was due at 6:00 PM and handed to you at 6:52 PM, 52 minutes late. For deliveries 45 minutes or more late, the credit is 20% of the subtotal. 20% of $128.00 is $25.60, but the most we can give on a Plus order is $25, so you get $25.00.\n\n**#6502 \u2013 Pho Real (Thursday): $5.00 credit added**\nIt was due at 7:15 PM and arrived at 7:45 PM, 30 minutes late. For Plus orders 16 to 44 minutes late, the credit is $5.00.\n\n**#6503 \u2013 Taqueria Luz (Tuesday): no credit**\nAt 5:50 PM, 40 minutes before the original 6:30 PM time, we sent you a push notification moving the delivery time to 7:00 PM because of a courier shortage. Your order was handed over at 7:12 PM, 12 minutes after that time. An order only counts as late if it arrives more than 15 minutes after the delivery time, so this one doesn't qualify.\n\n**#6504 \u2013 Burger Barn (last Friday, Oct 16): no credit**\nThis order was late, but it was delivered 8 days ago. We can only compensate late deliveries for up to 7 days after delivery, so this one is too old. I'm sorry about that.\n\n**In total, I added $30.00 to your account**, and it will be used automatically on your next orders. We give account credit for late deliveries, not refunds to your card.\n\nThank you for being a Plus member for two years. I'm sorry this week fell short. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for checking all four. I'm not happy about #6503 and #6504 though. For #6503, I got a notification at 5:50 about a 7:00 time, but I wasn't told that the order was still 12 minutes late against the new time, and I'd like to know why that doesn't count. Why doesn't it qualify? And for #6504, I don't think I should lose out just because I didn't get to it sooner.\n\nAlso, Thursday's #6502 was missing the summer rolls. Those were paid for and never arrived, so I'd like account credit for them."
  },
