  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand you're frustrated. Here's why those two orders don't qualify, and what I did about the summer rolls.\n\n**#6503 \u2013 why it doesn't count as late**\nWhen we send a new delivery time at least 30 minutes before the original one, the new time becomes the delivery time. Your notification came at 5:50 PM, 40 minutes before the original 6:30 PM time, so the delivery time became 7:00 PM. An order counts as late only if it arrives more than 15 minutes after the delivery time. Yours arrived 12 minutes after 7:00 PM, which is inside that window. I know it still felt slow, but under our rules it wasn't late.\n\n**#6504 \u2013 the time limit**\nWe can only compensate a late delivery for up to 7 days after it's delivered. #6504 was delivered on October 16 at 8:00 PM, so the deadline was October 23 at 8:00 PM, yesterday evening. I'm sorry, but I can't make an exception to that.\n\n**#6502 \u2013 missing summer rolls: $9.00 refunded to your card**\nYou reported this within our 48-hour window, so the summer rolls are covered. I couldn't give it as credit, though. The credit would have been $10.80 (the $9.00 price plus 20%), and with the $30.00 in late-delivery credit from earlier, that would put you over the $40 limit on credit per conversation. In that case I have to refund the item to your card. I've refunded **$9.00 to your Visa ending 4242**, which should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n\n**Summary of today**\n- $30.00 account credit for the late deliveries (#6501 and #6502)\n- $9.00 refunded to your card for the missing summer rolls (#6502)\n\nIf you'd like a specialist to review any of this, I can pass it to one. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I see the reasoning for #6503 and #6504, even if I don't love it. I'm fine with the $9.00 going back to my card for the rolls, that's acceptable. I'd still like someone to look at #6504 since I only found out it was late after the fact, but I don't need to escalate today. Thanks for going through everything."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks for working through all of this with me, Ms. Laurent. I haven't escalated #6504. If you decide you want a specialist to review it, just contact us and ask to speak to a person, and we'll pass it on. I can't say what the outcome would be.\n\n**What was done today:**\n- **$30.00 account credit** for late orders: $25.00 for #6501 and $5.00 for #6502. It will be used automatically on your next orders.\n- **$9.00 refunded to your Visa ending 4242** for the missing summer rolls on #6502. It should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n\nI'm sorry again for the late deliveries this week. Enjoy the rest of your evening!"
  }
